    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0081" n="71" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg71"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.85/2–145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Chinese
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Vincent</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Chief of the Shipping Division</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Saugstad</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-03-26">March 26, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reference is made to your memorandum of March 19, 1945<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d43-f1"/> attaching a memorandum of February 1, 1945 from the War
                    Shipping Administration and your reply of March 20, 1945,<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d43-f2"/> in regard to the allocation of additional merchant vessels
                    to China.</p>
                <p>CA perceives no objection to the proposal of the War Shipping Administration to
                    allocate a few additional merchant vessels to the properly authorized Chinese
                    authorities on a “bare-boat out, time-charter <pb facs="0082" n="72"
                        xml:id="pg72"/> back” basis, but feels that the State Department should be
                    consulted in the event that consideration is given to the sale or other final
                    disposal of such American vessels to China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ohn</hi>] C[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >arter</hi>] V[<hi rendition="#small-caps">incent</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d43-f1" n="5" xml:id="d43-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it stated: “We understand from Mr. Morse that the Navy Department
                    has no objection to the proposal.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d43-f2" n="6" xml:id="d43-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see footnote 59, <ref target="#pg43">p. 43</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
